From 0108e4e34b1bf2bdb1b6917db95f4ddd6a160a76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tannevaled <tannevaled@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:00:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cmd/internal/obj/loong64: add vector FMA, accept -2048 in
 vldrepl loads

Add the LSX and LASX floating-point fused multiply-add family:

	VFMADDD	Va, Vk, Vj, Vd	// vfmadd.d  vd, vj, vk, va
	XVFMADDD	Xa, Xk, Xj, Xd	// xvfmadd.d xd, xj, xk, xa

and likewise VFMSUB, VFNMADD, VFNMSUB, with F for .s and D for .d,
16 instructions in all. The operands are in the order of the scalar
FMADDD Fa, Fk, Fj, Fd, and the instructions share the VSHUFB/XVSHUFB
four-register optab entries.

The [X]vldrepl.{b,h,w,d} broadcast loads (VMOVQ off(Rj), Vd.<T> and
XVMOVQ off(Rj), Xd.<T>) take a signed 12-bit byte offset, stored in
units of the element size: si12, si11<<1, si10<<2, si9<<3. Every
element size reaches -2048, but the optab matched only C_SOREG_12,
and BIG_12 is 2046, so C_SOREG_12 holds [-2046, 2045]. -2048 was
classified as C_SOREG_16 and refused as an illegal combination for
all four element sizes, and so were the top of the .b range (2046,
2047) and of the .h range (2046). Match C_SOREG_16 instead and check
the range and alignment for each element size when encoding.

All new encodings were checked against llvm-mc (LLVM 22.1.5,
--triple=loongarch64 -mattr=+lasx): 74 new lines in loong64enc1.s,
including the minimum and maximum offset of each element size for
both VMOVQ and XVMOVQ, and every register field at 0 and 31 for
VFMADDD and XVFMADDD. 12 new lines in loong64error.s cover offsets
one element past either end, and misalignment.

An independent check, go-asmgen's gap checker (goasmgap verify -require),
assembles the reference cases it holds for vfmadd.d, xvfmadd.d,
vldrepl.d and xvldrepl.d, produced by GNU as 2.43 on a Loongson
3C5000L, and finds 32 of 32 identical; before this change it reported
VFMADDD and XVFMADDD absent and the two .d loads at 7/8, refusing
-2048. llvm-mc agrees with GNU as on all 32.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
